    {
      "name": "E multi-tab comparison",
      "model": "qwen2.5:3b",
      "status": "complete",
      "output": "The pilot study and the replication study examined the impact of gardens on water use. The pilot study conducted among 42 volunteers saw a 12% reduction in water use over six weeks, but it did not use a randomized control group. In contrast, the replication study, which was a twelve-week randomized trial with 210 gardens, found a 2% reduction in water use, with results showing a 3% to 7% reduction in water use. While the replication study did not establish a clear benefit, it used a more rigorous study design, suggesting greater validity.",
